WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.807 --> 00:00:01.689
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.862 --> 00:00:07.293
My name is Aishwarya Srinivasan and I am an AI and ML innovation leader here at IBM.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:13.920
What we see in the current knowledge era is that&nbsp;
the volume of data has increased tremendously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:20.640
but the amount of information extracted from the&nbsp;
data hasn’t increased as much, which leads to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:27.600
knowledge gap with the un-used data. The total&nbsp;
accumulated volume of data has grown from 4.4ZB&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:39.760
in 2013 to 44ZB in 2020, so we accumulated 9&nbsp;
times more data just in those 7 years, but we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:46.560
haven’t been leveraging all this data. This data&nbsp;
can be anywhere. Different industries, different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:54.160
organizations, local businesses, individuals&nbsp;
store their data in various sources - Oracle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:01.360
Db2, SQL Server, PostgreSQL, MongoDB etc.&nbsp;
that could be residing on multiple platforms;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:10.320
cloud, on-premises, and mainframes in various&nbsp;
formats; relational, non-relational and NoSQL.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.360
The challenge comes when we want to use&nbsp;
all these data sources for analytics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:21.760
and to build models. So, what’s the best&nbsp;
way to move data? To not move it at all.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:26.320
This is where Data Virtualization comes into play.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:33.120
Data virtualization is a technique to connect&nbsp;
to all data sources seamlessly and securely in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:41.440
a single location. With these capabilities, we can&nbsp;
query all the data source as if they reside in one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.760
single space. without having to copy and replicate&nbsp;
data, regardless of its format. This would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:51.520
significantly reduce costs and complexity for data&nbsp;
engineering, simplify data management, improve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.840
collaboration from data stewards to engineers to&nbsp;
data scientist, and enable centralized access.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.120
When working with such huge volumes of data,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:03.840
governance also comes into play which is&nbsp;
also addressed with data virtualization.&nbsp;

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:09.200
As an overview, Data virtualization&nbsp;
consists of three layers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.360
The bottom most is the connection layer that&nbsp;
interacts with the databases that we need.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:23.360
Next is the virtualization layer that is used to&nbsp;
build optimized queries, virtual tables and scale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:29.200
while preserving performance with parallel&nbsp;
processing. The third layer is the consumer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:36.720
layer which has all the user interface through&nbsp;
while once can build views and query them. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:43.000
a complementary layer, we have the governance&nbsp;
catalog, that pulls metadata from across the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:49.840
data sources and builds on business terms, data&nbsp;
lineage, data privacy and protection rules.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:57.280
With this we can have a controlled, governed&nbsp;
and secure access to virtual datasets.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.640
Let’s dig a little deeper into this.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:06.204
With Data Virtualization, we can achieve faster&nbsp;
Data Exploration. Data virtualization is designed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.204 --> 00:03:06.335
and architected as a peer-to-peer computational&nbsp;
mesh, which offers a significant advantage over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.335 --> 00:03:06.431
traditional federation architecture.&nbsp;
Using IBM Research advancements,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.431 --> 00:03:06.561
the data virtualization engine can rapidly deliver&nbsp;
query results from multiple data sources by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.561 --> 00:03:07.840
leveraging advanced parallel processing&nbsp;
and optimization. Collaborative highly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:12.880
paralleled compute models provide superior&nbsp;
query performance compared to federation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:19.235
up to 430% faster against 100TB&nbsp;
datasets. Data virtualization has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.235 --> 00:03:19.680
unmatched scaling of complex queries with joins&nbsp;
and aggregates across dozens of live systems.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:23.600
Secondly, when running queries&nbsp;
on these datasets, we need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:26.541
to build optimized versions for better modeling.
Machine learning can make database queries faster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.541 --> 00:03:26.663
and improve outcomes. For example, a traditional&nbsp;
cost-based query optimizer can provide a suggested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.663 --> 00:03:26.785
execution strategy for a given query, but if the&nbsp;
strategy doesn’t work as expected, the optimizer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.785 --> 00:03:26.896
can’t learn from the experience. However, a&nbsp;
machine learning-powered query optimizer can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.896 --> 00:03:27.016
learn from experience and refine the query path&nbsp;
with each execution. That’s how the Db2 Machine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.016 --> 00:03:28.160
Learning Optimizer works. It mimics neural network&nbsp;
patterns to optimize query paths. The result is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:32.000
faster insights to your team—with&nbsp;
some queries being completed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.560
up to 8 – 10 times faster as&nbsp;
measured by IBM internal testing.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.725
Third is Cost saving. To run a business in a&nbsp;
data-centric environment, you must have access&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.725 --> 00:03:38.947
to exactly what you need, when you need it. When&nbsp;
business users have responsive and proactive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.947 --> 00:03:40.720
access to all data with governance, they make&nbsp;
better business decisions. Data virtualization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:46.160
leads to significantly lower costs for&nbsp;
infrastructure and reduces time spent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:50.720
managing data, which has a direct&nbsp;
effect on organizations bottom line.&nbsp;

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:51.269
Another cost savings of the platform comes in&nbsp;
the form of the high-level compression techniques&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.269 --> 00:03:56.640
within Virtual Data Pipeline. This solution helps&nbsp;
enterprises minimize the required storage of data&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:01.280
copies while still maintaining continuity&nbsp;
between the compressed and optimized versions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.024
of the source or production data. The first copy&nbsp;
typically sees around a 50 percent decrease in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.024 --> 00:04:03.524
size while subsequent copies can garner upwards of&nbsp;
95 percent decrease from the original source data.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:10.560
Finally, Virtual Data Pipeline can be used&nbsp;
as a storage backup and recovery capability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:14.800
and expands to cover test data&nbsp;
management and analytics data&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:15.555
pipeline. Many organizations are shifting their&nbsp;
application strategy to a continuous approach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:15.782
to ensure quality and support agile development&nbsp;
and DevOps. For test data, this means drastically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.782 --> 00:04:16.000
reducing the data provisioning time while enabling&nbsp;
automation and self-service access to data.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.480
So, with Data Virtualization&nbsp;
organizations can view, access,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:25.767
manipulate and analyze data, without&nbsp;
worrying about the physical location.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.000
To learn more about Data&nbsp;
Virtualization, do visit our website.

